.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-offbox-run 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-offbox\-run \- Run this session\*(Aqs off\-box daemon until it is killed: push when there is something new, wait when the forge says to
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten offbox run\fR [\fB\-\-transcript\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-session\fR> <\fB\-\-harness\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run this session\*(Aqs off\-box daemon until it is killed: push when there is something new, wait when the forge says to
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-session\fR \fI<session>\fR
The harness\*(Aqs own identifier for the session whose state is pushed
.TP
\fB\-\-harness\fR \fI<harness>\fR
The harness the session belongs to; it selects where the session\*(Aqs records are read from
.TP
\fB\-\-transcript\fR \fI<transcript>\fR
The transcript path the harness named for this session, where it named one
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
